	<text xml:lang="la">
		<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" subtype="metadata" n="1">Siehe dazu <bibl source="b19">HBBW XVI</bibl> 96f, Anm. 1.</note>
		<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" subtype="metadata" n="2">Das Jahr ergibt sich aus dem Briefinhalt.</note>
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Mirabitur fortassis amplitudo tua, qua audatia fretus hoc <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>tibi negotium iniungere audeam.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Verum cum herus<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3"><persName ref="p6355">Hieronymus Sailer</persName>.</note> meus tua <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>familiaritate iamdudum se usum cum magna suavitate affirmet <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>et <persName ref="p8032">Franciscum Dryandrum Hispanum</persName><note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4"><persName ref="p8032">Francisco de Enzinas</persName>, der damals in <placeName ref="l28">Basel</placeName> wohnte und Ende August/Anfang September 1546 in <placeName ref="l587">Zürich</placeName> gewesen war; s. <bibl source="b20">HBBW XVII</bibl> 361, Anm. 2.</note> amicum habeas, non dubito <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>ex utriusque iussu meas ad te literas <placeName ref="l28">Basileam</placeName> mittendas<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Ein Auszug dieses Briefes von <persName ref="p8311">Claudius</persName> an <persName ref="p8032">Enzinas</persName> wird in <ref target="file12749">Nr. 2702</ref>,23-30, zitiert.</note> mittere, <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>quod scio eorum te gratia et libenter et quam primum facere.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div2" corresp="regest2">
				<p>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z7"/>Nova iubet te dominus ex <persName ref="p8071">Joanne Voglero</persName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6"><persName ref="p8071">Hans Vogler d.Ä.</persName>; s. unten Z. 14.</note>, cive vestro, perquirere, <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>ad quem pridiae<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">=pridie.</note> scripsit.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Principum<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Kurfürst <persName ref="p19065">Johann Friedrich I. von Sachsen</persName> und Landgraf <persName ref="p3590">Philipp von Hessen</persName>. - Sie hatten das Lager bei <placeName ref="l171">Giengen an der Brenz</placeName> am 22. November aufgehoben; s. <ref target="file12709">Nr. 2662</ref>, Anm. 20.</note> discessus nunciatur satis <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>constanter.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Elector enim <placeName ref="l749">Saxoniae</placeName> necesse magis habet sua defendere <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>et propulsare iniuriam domi illatam, quam foras aliis inferre.<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Zu verstehen: manus (bzw. bellum) aliis inferre.</note></s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z11"/>Dux enim <persName ref="p18250">Mauritius</persName><note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Herzog <persName ref="p18250">Moritz von Sachsen</persName>.</note> magnis copiis ex <placeName ref="l2449">Bohemis</placeName> et levis armaturae <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>latronibus (quas vulgo <foreign xml:lang="de">hussern<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">Husaren. - Es handelte sich um kroatische, walachische und polnische Reiter. Man sah in ihnen Hunnen, <placeName ref="l882">Ungarn</placeName>, <placeName ref="l2510">Türken</placeName> und die Völker Gog und Magog verkörpert; s. <hi>Voigt, Moritz</hi> 213, und vgl. <hi><persName ref="p8032">Enzinas</persName> BW</hi> 188, Nr. 23b, wo sie als "Hunnos equites" erscheinen.</note></foreign> appellamus)<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>Klammern</hi> ergänzt.</note> conflatis vastat eius <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>regionem et pleraque iam oppida occupavit ex-<pb type="edition" next="352"/>cepta <placeName ref="l558">Viteberga</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>et <placeName ref="l1571">Gotha</placeName>.<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Siehe dazu <bibl source="b667">Voigt, Moritz</bibl> 225-228. 241.</note></s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Quo consilio vel animo, id nondum est compertum.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z15"/>Reliqua communicabit <persName ref="p8455">Voglerus</persName> senior.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div3" corresp="regest3">
				<p>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Vale.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Calendis decembris.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z16"/><persName ref="p8311">Mathias Clodius</persName>, filiorum<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13"><persName ref="p20873">Bartholomäus</persName> und <persName ref="p6357">Anton Sailer</persName>; s. <bibl source="b19">HBBW XVI</bibl> 96f, Anm. 1.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z17"/><persName ref="p6355">Hieronimi Sayleri</persName> praeceptor, <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>tuae amplitudinis addictissimus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Amplissimo ornatissimoque <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>viro <persName ref="p495">Henricho Bullingero</persName>, <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>ecclesiae dei apud <placeName ref="l587">Tygurum</placeName> <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>a contionibus, domino suo <lb xml:id="p2z5"/>et patrono plurimum <lb xml:id="p2z6"/>observando.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l587">Tyguri</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
	</text>
